Appendix A Stage 1 clean year-length ceiling 5778-ന്റെ നാല് അടുത്ത boundary values explicit ആയി പരിശോധിക്കുന്ന probe. historical 5781 legacy constant ഇവിടെ ഉണ്ടാകരുത്; 5778 മാത്രം accepted, 5779, 5780, 5781 rejected. outputs ക്രമത്തിൽ `1,0,0,0`.

Hamlet, clean maximum 5778 സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Juliet, current candidate length സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Romeo, acceptance boolean സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Othello, നാല് boundary rows-ന്റെ counter സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Prospero, assignment, comparison, output സഹായിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.

Act I: clean maximum.

Scene I: 5778 exact binary sum ആയി നിർമ്മിക്കുന്നു.
[Enter Prospero and Hamlet]
Prospero:
 You are a big big big big big big big big big big big big hero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a big big big big big big big big big big hero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a big big big big big big big big big hero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a big big big big big big big hero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a big big big big hero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a big hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Hamlet and Juliet]
Hamlet: You are as good as Hamlet.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Othello]
Prospero: You are a hero.
[Exeunt]

Act II: four adjacent candidate lengths.

Scene I: stop after four rows.
[Enter Othello and Prospero]
Othello: Am I better than a big big hero?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to act III.
[Exeunt]

Scene II: default reject; accept only current <= 5778.
[Enter Prospero and Romeo]
Prospero: You are nothing.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Juliet and Hamlet]
Juliet: Am I better than Hamlet?
Hamlet: If so, let us proceed to scene IV.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Romeo]
Prospero: You are a hero.

Scene IV: output boolean and advance current length.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Romeo]
Prospero: Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Juliet]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Othello]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero. Let us return to scene I.
[Exeunt]

Act III: done.

Scene I: no extra output.
